{"posts":[{"id":"bsz_p1_1","t":"The BSZ is a wonderful and very simple trick we can profit greatly from.\n\nThe lesson is short, but its implication is BIG!\n\nYou can find the lesson in Markepedia, or from this LINK","a":"—","d":"","n":"#1","p":1,"im":[],"m":1},{"id":"bsz_p1_2","t":"Ifmyante wrote: The BSZ is a wonderful and very simple trick we can profit greatly from.\n\nThe lesson is short, but its implication is BIG!\n\nYou can find the lesson in Markepedia, or from this LINK\n\npast\n\nThanks IF very helpfull - but where is the target? Next opposing BSZ zone with clean orders?\n\nHans","a":"—","d":"","n":"#2","p":1,"im":[],"m":2},{"id":"bsz_p1_3","t":"Al3cs\n\nWhat about this?","a":"—","d":"","n":"#3","p":1,"im":[],"m":3},{"id":"bsz_p1_4","t":"2144","a":"—","d":"","n":"#4","p":1,"im":["dad4798787087f0c4f92557c9e270561bbf79664","6b7a3189b64b82496d4732fb813d92dee6e504e2","0189dbafd144741fee8062b2ec1290935b1f4634","50e0dabc8f4ad11eb1eca55f5ff93875f2ff3a1b","8934be0b7cda7801e339dcdaa4ba93fccdfc8114","85ff1f040ef690728681ed19afd05522f82e6a4b","bf6750a6685f021d545f2c9a90525ff70ed7f4d9","8e6880dba92c5e6c472b82f05d276327fbf7c594","74f8bf9eddbb7a1ce390b73c53215df42577fd76","4b91c495b4a20c6b7ec4dbaf637fb28e309afcba","94bcaa3e3659fb06a01bd0a24566ba3a3788b77c"],"m":4},{"id":"bsz_p1_5","t":"Al3cs\n\nRight now on your screens","a":"—","d":"","n":"#5","p":1,"im":[],"m":5},{"id":"bsz_p1_6","t":"Kavya\n\nYes, I started it for doing homework, but then I ended up looking into CPs or FL followed by Best Buy/Sell @ Caps. or actually giving real BOs.\n\nSo yes till I don't satisfy I will keep it away and will trade based on what is really simple. QM! or MPL!\n\nBut yes I also like OOM so much!","a":"—","d":"","n":"#6","p":1,"im":[],"m":6},{"id":"bsz_p1_7","t":"hansma wrote:\n\nIfmyante wrote: The BSZ is a wonderful and very simple trick we can profit greatly from.\n\nThe lesson is short, but its implication is BIG!\n\nWasher\n\nfind\n\nHave a think about where to look for trades while doing the homework","a":"—","d":"","n":"#7","p":1,"im":[],"m":7},{"id":"bsz_p1_8","t":"Thank you IF for the new lesson.\n\nMy first try on BSZ.\n\nI also have a question regarding the iQM in the above image. I have marked two red rectangles. The first one I marked as it shows an aggressive price drop assuming it is a good supply. And the second red box is a result of engulfing the previous red box. I have asked my question in the image below. In HTF that iQM seems to be valid but in LTF, it is not.\n\nWill you be able to tell me if we need to consider LTF FLs when when we check the validity of a QM?\n\nThanks in advance.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#8","p":1,"im":["daf7d70abefd73a7e66cfcd45e034c3b0345493d","ecea4e1b3c55b3b697ea9806f206199971cdf42d"],"m":8},{"id":"bsz_p1_9","t":"Al3cs wrote: Right now on your screens\n\npast\n\nMaybe but dont see any room down also dont like the spikes above IQM","a":"—","d":"","n":"#9","p":1,"im":["22e429be285a7f9c1257eeecddc2a6b4d3429a8d"],"m":9},{"id":"bsz_p1_10","t":"GGJJ\n\nHere is my thought. Your BSZ in the bottom is a good one. I think there is also one on the top.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#10","p":1,"im":["7b44e31be981d189d15af27b85dc4128783dc275"],"m":10},{"id":"bsz_p1_11","t":"","a":"—","d":"","n":"#11","p":1,"im":["e3c37392863ac8f9a09d8090809fffde0394547d"],"m":11},{"id":"bsz_p1_12","t":"linos\n\nhadnt yet seen this thread when I made this chart for practise, thanks again!","a":"—","d":"","n":"#12","p":1,"im":["bba0caa9dda0d01c5aa1b51fe98b443342647527"],"m":12},{"id":"bsz_p1_13","t":"Al3cs\n\nhansma wrote:\n\nAl3cs wrote: Right now on your screens\n\nIMO it can well move down after the ENG we had last friday\n\nand I think I took my best entry ever, but we all know, that the exit is more important than the entry\n\nExcuse me all for the off topic","a":"—","d":"","n":"#13","p":1,"im":["22e429be285a7f9c1257eeecddc2a6b4d3429a8d"],"m":13},{"id":"bsz_p1_14","t":"Al3cs\n\nAnother one, around 1.0600 which is a nice historical level. This was easy to spot after the fact but surely I would miss it in real time\n\nMain view","a":"—","d":"","n":"#14","p":1,"im":[],"m":14},{"id":"bsz_p1_15","t":"","a":"—","d":"","n":"#15","p":1,"im":["84313e8493379d8a86cfdd810a8284876fe733eb"],"m":15},{"id":"bsz_p1_16","t":"Al3cs\n\nAl3cs wrote: Another one, around 1.0600 which is a nice historical level. This was easy to spot after the fact but surely I would miss it in real time\n\nThis is something I will investigate more: I set a PO on the higher BSZ / 2T level but price reacted at the lower 2T level. I will investigate to understand if is simply confuence or something more.","a":"—","d":"","n":"#16","p":1,"im":[],"m":16},{"id":"bsz_p1_17","t":"","a":"—","d":"","n":"#17","p":1,"im":["2f57c8d8c6d29a699b3caa39e0a1b9b6af092c3a"],"m":17},{"id":"bsz_p1_18","t":"hi Alecs,\n\na different opinion, hopefully can complement each other.\n\n2144","a":"—","d":"","n":"#18","p":1,"im":["b45a95a505dd8e50ab4fcb97b3e70e89f952058a","09c09ed6fbaeae55f3590d8ea9bbe0ee5ae1cdb1"],"m":18},{"id":"bsz_p1_19","t":"Agree with Alan on the BSZ. I'm just thinking they are going to do more tricks before reaching there. like these here maybe....\n\n2144","a":"—","d":"","n":"#19","p":1,"im":["b18c43fd46c3f13a8194534d5c9f65182adc9ff8","f638a5723e264ce5aa3ff0d4b964fa99e6afbbc1"],"m":19},{"id":"bsz_p1_20","t":"That was what I meant by (increasing the price >> cleaning the orders and then FO to lower) ^_^","a":"—","d":"","n":"#20","p":1,"im":[],"m":20},{"id":"bsz_p1_21","t":"The BSZ lesson isn't complete.\n\nI'm trying to work out a way to get the reader to get the first bit of the lesson, then work try to work out the rest of it before being shown how I see it. Needs some thought.....\n\nAnyway, I'd like you to consider the lesson, and, from chart research, work\n\nWasher\n\nout how the BSZ can be traded. From where to where? TT or PAC? Allow for runners? Stops and other management.\n\nIt's all there on the charts, and soon enough I'll find an home for the lesson\n\nKavya, madhuri, Enlightenme, pratihar, alirezat, Shantala, Canadough\n\nfind\n\n14517","a":"—","d":"","n":"#21","p":1,"im":[],"m":21},{"id":"bsz_p1_22","t":"Kavya","a":"—","d":"","n":"#22","p":1,"im":["622000fe36f348c01798b442cc4a32d5c23fb826"],"m":22},{"id":"bsz_p1_23","t":"Kavya\n\nIfmyante wrote: The BSZ lesson isn't complete.\n\nI'm trying to work out a way to get the reader to get the first bit of the lesson, then work try to work out the rest of it before being shown how I see it. Needs some thought.....","a":"—","d":"","n":"#23","p":1,"im":[],"m":23},{"id":"bsz_p1_24","t":"Manu\n\nMaybe this?\n\nAnother one:","a":"—","d":"","n":"#24","p":1,"im":["dfc9c2c9d622613aa4a0cc6262d6a3d09fc26f55","b9d8b1100b428f95ef846057d4d38bfa17dec167","477fdfb2c1b2f3101add307456e72a43839815b3"],"m":24},{"id":"bsz_p1_25","t":"Kavya\n\nManu wrote: Maybe this?","a":"—","d":"","n":"#25","p":1,"im":["dfc9c2c9d622613aa4a0cc6262d6a3d09fc26f55"],"m":25}],"images":[{"k":"dad4798787087f0c4f92557c9e270561bbf79664","t":"assets/thumbs/dad4798787087f0c4f92557c9e270561bbf79664.webp","f":"assets/images/dad4798787087f0c4f92557c9e270561bbf79664.png","w":1800,"h":973,"b":606521,"o":"dad4798787087f0c4f92557c9e270561bbf79664.png","p":1,"pid":"bsz_p1_4"},{"k":"6b7a3189b64b82496d4732fb813d92dee6e504e2","t":"assets/thumbs/6b7a3189b64b82496d4732fb813d92dee6e504e2.webp","f":"assets/images/6b7a3189b64b82496d4732fb813d92dee6e504e2.png","w":1800,"h":973,"b":526479,"o":"6b7a3189b64b82496d4732fb813d92dee6e504e2.png","p":1,"pid":"bsz_p1_4"},{"k":"0189dbafd144741fee8062b2ec1290935b1f4634","t":"assets/thumbs/0189dbafd144741fee8062b2ec1290935b1f4634.webp","f":"assets/images/0189dbafd144741fee8062b2ec1290935b1f4634.png","w":1800,"h":973,"b":533025,"o":"0189dbafd144741fee8062b2ec1290935b1f4634.png","p":1,"pid":"bsz_p1_4"},{"k":"50e0dabc8f4ad11eb1eca55f5ff93875f2ff3a1b","t":"assets/thumbs/50e0dabc8f4ad11eb1eca55f5ff93875f2ff3a1b.webp","f":"assets/images/50e0dabc8f4ad11eb1eca55f5ff93875f2ff3a1b.png","w"